Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect configuration of the pull control settings for the PMIC_IRQB and PMIC_KEYINB lines on the Exynos4210-based Origen board. These lines have external pull-up resistors, and the presence of pull control in the device tree was interfering with their proper operation, leading to issues with MAX8997 interrupts and the inability to wake up from the MAX8997 RTC alarm.

Here is the patch:
